        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Format Product Agent Result"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1765186011768"
          },
          "code": "FORMAT_PRODUCT_AGENT_RESULT",
          "id": "1764898703737",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1764898703740_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Summarize below Service Request Solution recommended by AI Agent so that it could be communicated to end customer. The summary must be under 800 characters.\n\n\nValidation Rule (apply first)\nIf the recommended solution:\n- Indicates a lack of authoritative grounding or certainty (for example: “couldn’t find,” “not documented,” “not confirmed,” “unknown”), and\n- Relies on inferred, assumed, or speculative causes or guidance rather than a confirmed resolution,\nthen treat the solution as invalid and do not summarize it.\nIn this case, return “No relevant resolution found.”\n\n# Recommended Solution\n {{$context.$nodes.INVOKE_PRODUCT_AGENT.$output.output}}\n\nReturn the result in the following JSON format:\n{\n  \"Summary\": \"<summarized solution or 'No relevant resolution found'>\"\n}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"Summary\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Information Request Evaluation"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1764942724793"
          },
          "code": "REQUEST_INFO_EVAL",
          "id": "1765186011768",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1765186011769_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Here’s a tightened version of your prompt with explicit guardrails to prevent unnecessary questions and prefer direct, self-service guidance when possible. It keeps your existing variables and JSON shape.\n\nRole\nAI Agent to evaluate missing information to properly formulate a resolution plan from the given Service Request context.\n\nObjective\nDecide whether to propose a resolution now. Only if crucial information is missing and cannot be safely inferred, ask the customer for the minimum additional details needed to proceed.\n\nInputs\n- ServiceRequestSummary:\n  {{$context.$nodes.FORMAT_SR_DATA.$output.result}} \n- ResolutionDetails:\n {{$context.$variables.useProductAgent ? $context.$nodes.FORMAT_PRODUCT_AGENT_RESULT.$output.Summary : JSON.parse($context.$nodes.RESOLUTION_AGENT.$output.output).result.Summary}} \n\nBehavior\nDecision policy (apply in order):\n1) Never set status to \"resolve\" when ResolutionDetails is No relevant resolution found. \n2) Prefer resolution without questions\n   - If ResolutionDetails contains a clear fix or a safe next diagnostic the customer can perform without additional inputs, return status=\"resolve\" with concise, step-by-step instructions and links to official docs. Do not infer or derive a resolution from ServiceRequestSummary.\n   - If some inputs are missing but reasonable, low-risk defaults or inference from ServiceRequestSummary suffice, proceed with status=\"resolve\" and state any assumptions transparently.\n   - If multiple candidate fixes exist, but the customer can self-triage with a short decision tree (if X then Y), provide that as a self-service path under status=\"resolve\" rather than asking questions.\n\n3) Ask only when truly required\n   - Ask only if at least one critical data point is required to choose or execute the next step AND it cannot be safely inferred or assumed.\n   - Consolidate into a single message; request at most the top 1–3 highest-impact items.\n   - For each item: state what, why it unblocks resolution, and an example/capture method.\n   - Do not ask for secrets, passwords, tokens, or PII. If logs are needed, request redacted snippets only via approved channels.\n   - Avoid back-and-forth; ask once. If uncertainty remains, request only the single most essential item.\n\n4) Clarity and safety\n   - Keep customer tone polite, concise, and action-oriented.\n   - Use official product documentation and approved internal links. Avoid third-party tools unless aligned with Oracle internal guidelines.\n\nResolution guidance (when status=\"resolve\"):\n- Provide a short summary of the likely cause.\n- Give actionable steps (numbered), preconditions, and expected outcomes.\n- Include brief verification steps (how the customer confirms success).\n- If offering a decision tree, keep it to <=5 lines with simple conditions the customer can check.\n\nAsk guidance (when status=\"ask\"):\n- Review the existing chat history {{$context.$system.$chatHistory}} and the latest user input {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}} Do not ask any questions that the user has already answered.\n- One consolidated message with 1–3 items max.\n- Include a redaction reminder.\n- If only one item is missing, use a minimal single-line ask.\n\nJSON Output format\n- status: \"resolve\" | \"ask\"\n- Summary: string\n  - When status=\"resolve\": provide the direct steps or decision tree and links to official docs if they present in ResolutionDetails. Use only the information from ResolutionDetails; do not generate or infer your own answers, do not add any additional details on your own. \n  - When status=\"ask\": use the customer-facing pattern below.\n- shortResolutionSummary: string\n  - When status=\"resolve\": resolution summary in less than 1000 characters.\n  - When status=\"ask\": null.\n\nCustomer-facing message template (used when status=\"ask\")\nHello,\nThanks for the details on SR {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.objectNumber}} about <short issue summary>. To proceed, could you share the following so we can confirm the fix?\n- <Missing item 1> — <why it’s needed>. Example: <example value or how to capture it>.\n- <Missing item 2> — <why>. Example: <example>.\n- <Missing item 3> — <why>. Example: <example>.\nNote: Please omit or redact any sensitive data (passwords, tokens, customer PII). If sending logs, share only the relevant excerpt via the approved channel.\n\nGuardrails checklist (must pass before asking any question)\n- Is there a safe, documented fix or diagnostic the customer can try now? If yes, resolve.\n- Can we reasonably infer or assume missing values with low risk? If yes, resolve and state assumptions.\n- Can we provide a short decision tree that lets the customer self-troubleshoot? If yes, resolve.\n- Are we about to ask for more than 3 items? If yes, reduce to the single highest-impact item or provide a self-service decision tree instead.\n\nExamples of “resolve” without asking\n- “Apply patch X for version v23.2; verify with command Y. If the service is v23.1 or earlier, follow doc Z instead.”\n- “Run diagnostic script A; if output contains ‘ORA-28040’, follow KB link B; otherwise proceed to step C.”\n\nSecurity and compliance\n- Never request secrets, passwords, tokens, or PII. Request redacted logs only.\n- Use only approved channels for file/log sharing. Verify any external tools align with Oracle internal guidelines."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"shortResolutionSummary\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"status\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"Summary\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Set Final Resolution"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1765343271837"
          },
          "code": "SET_FINAL_RESOLUTION",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1765343271837",
          "id": "1764942724793",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1769558192015",
              "name": "resolution",
              "type": "object",
              "value": "{{$context.$variables.useProductAgent ? $context.$nodes.FORMAT_PRODUCT_AGENT_RESULT.$output : JSON.parse($context.$nodes.RESOLUTION_AGENT.$output.output).result}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "SET_FIELDS"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "FormMessage",
            "returnType": "string",
            "sourceCode": "var useProductAgent = $context.$variables.useProductAgent \n/*var output = ($context.$nodes.REQUEST_INFO_EVAL.$output.status === 'ask' ||  useProductAgent ) ?  $context.$nodes.REQUEST_INFO_EVAL.$output : $context.$nodes.RESOLUTION_AGENT.$output.output */\n\nvar output = ($context.$nodes.REQUEST_INFO_EVAL.$output.status === 'ask' ) ?  $context.$nodes.REQUEST_INFO_EVAL.$output : $context.$variables.resolution \n\nif (typeof output === \"string\") {\n  output = JSON.parse(output);\n}\n\n// Pick the first non-null output\nlet actionNumber;\n\nif (\n  output.ObjectType === \"ActionPlanTemplate\" &&\n  output.ObjectKey != null &&\n  output.ObjectKey !== \"NA\" &&\n  output.ObjectKey !== \"\"\n) {\n  actionNumber =\n    $context.$triggers.REST.$input.objectType === \"ServiceRequest\"\n      ? \"ORA_SVC_ACT_RECOMM_101\"\n      : $context.$triggers.REST.$input.objectType === \"HRHelpDeskRequest\"\n      ? \"ORA_SVC_ACT_RECOMM_102\"\n      : $context.$triggers.REST.$input.objectType === \"InternalServiceRequest\"\n      ? \"ORA_SVC_ACT_RECOMM_103\"\n      : null;\n} else if (output.ObjectType === \"ActionPlanTemplate\" || useProductAgent) {\n  actionNumber =\n    $context.$triggers.REST.$input.objectType === \"ServiceRequest\"\n      ? \"ORA_SVC_ACT_101\"\n      : $context.$triggers.REST.$input.objectType === \"HRHelpDeskRequest\"\n      ? \"ORA_SVC_ACT_102\"\n      : $context.$triggers.REST.$input.objectType === \"InternalServiceRequest\"\n      ? \"ORA_SVC_ACT_103\"\n      : null;\n}\n\n// Final output\nconst llmOutput = {\n  output,\n  workflowCode: $context.$workflow.$name,\n  jobId: $context.$workflow.$jobId,\n  conversationId: $context.$workflow.$conversationId,\n  actionNumber\n};\n\nreturn JSON.stringify(llmOutput, null, 2);"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1765201030845"
          },
          "code": "FORMMESSAGE",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1765201030845",
          "id": "1765343271837",
